# GitHub Access (this repo)

Repo: `hereisphil/2606-WDV349-CantuPhillip` (private). Owner account: **`hereisphil`** (`thereisphil@gmail.com`).

## Auth caveat

This machine may have multiple `gh` logins. A `GITHUB_TOKEN` / `GH_TOKEN` env var often forces **`phil-hgraph`**, which **cannot** see this private repo (API 404 / "Could not resolve").

For any `gh` API work (issues, PRs, checks, releases):

1. Unset the token override: `env -u GITHUB_TOKEN -u GH_TOKEN …`
2. Ensure active account is `hereisphil`: `gh auth switch --user hereisphil`
3. Then run the `gh` command

Example:

```bash
env -u GITHUB_TOKEN -u GH_TOKEN gh auth switch --user hereisphil
env -u GITHUB_TOKEN -u GH_TOKEN gh issue list -R hereisphil/2606-WDV349-CantuPhillip
```

## Git push/pull

SSH to `git@github.com` authenticates as **`hereisphil`** — `git push` / `git pull` on `origin` work without the `gh` workaround.

